+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. Committed changes are delivered using self-hosted WebSockets for low-latency updates without vendor coupling or recurring realtime service fees.
 
-Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery must be designed together after this choice. Polling would favor cursor queries; self-hosted sockets would need connection management and replay; hosted delivery would need publication reconciliation and provider credentials. Neither operating cost nor minimum operational burden has been declared the overriding criterion.
+Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery operate in concert around this delivery model:
+- The change store maintains replayable event revisions and reliable publication to support reconnection and delivery.
+- The delivery layer manages persistent WebSocket sessions, broadcasts revision notifications or delta payloads, and enforces connection capacity limits.
+- Browser sync maintains the WebSocket connection, detects drops, and handles reconnect and catch-up logic to restore current board state after disconnections.
 
